    -> status bit8 SET (up-ack residue): dom6 matches the
       powered dom0-5 baseline (probe 2026-08-20); only the
       fw-commanded dom7 differs (bit12 down-ack, state 0).
    -> ctrl = 0x00000000: no gate hold on any dom6 slot
       (bits 0/1/2 all clear). Boot value on this card was
       0x02 (slot 0x17's gate, held through every prior run);
       the 2026-08-25 --manual-powerup released it and the
       release PERSISTED across processes. A cold boot
       restores 0x02 -- the release lives only in the SMU
       session (re-run --manual-powerup after any cold cycle).
    -> rail = 0: IDLE -- the rail-up bit self-clears when the
       sequencer takes it, so 0 carries no state by itself
       (powered dom0-3 also read 0). MEASURED 2026-08-25: the
       rail-up store landed (the ctrl store in the same run
       did) yet moved nothing -- favored reading: an already-
       up rail consumed the one-shot instantly. The SMU-side
       power question is as settled as this oracle can make
       it; the VCN register block itself (the --direct-load
       POWER_STATUS MMIO read) is the arbiter.

